diff --git a/doc/signet-target-spacing.md b/doc/signet-target-spacing.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..7e779c9
--- /dev/null
+++ b/doc/signet-target-spacing.md
@@ -0,0 +1,53 @@
+# Difficulty retargets on a custom signet
+
+A signet keeps Bitcoin's difficulty adjustment. Every 2016 blocks the target is
+multiplied by the time the last period actually took over the time it was
+expected to take (`2016 * nPowTargetSpacing`, two weeks), with that ratio
+clamped to between a quarter and four. A custom signet whose blocks come faster
+than every ten minutes therefore has its difficulty raised at each retarget, by
+the full factor of four while a period takes less than a quarter of two weeks,
+until the proof of work on top of its producer's pause brings the average
+interval back up to ten minutes.
+
+`-signetpowtargetspacing=<seconds>[@<height>]` makes the retargets at or above
+`<height>` (default 0) measure each period against `<seconds>` per block
+instead, from 1 to 600. Nothing else changes: the retarget interval stays 2016
+blocks, the clamp stays a factor of four, and `nPowTargetSpacing` itself, which
+the node also uses for timeouts and estimates, stays 600. A signet that
+produces a block every `<seconds>` then keeps a steady difficulty; one that
+produces faster than that still has it raised. A `<height>` inside a retarget
+period takes effect at the next retarget.
+
+The option requires `-signetchallenge`, and it is a consensus rule of the
+network that uses it:
+
+- Every node must use the same values. A node without them, or with others,
+  computes a different target wherever the two rules differ, and rejects the
+  network's blocks from the first retarget where they do.
+- A network that already exists must give every node the option before the
+  chain reaches the first retarget it changes, the first multiple of 2016 at or
+  above `<height>`. The retargets below it were computed against 600 s and stay
+  valid; the first one it changes has to be produced under it.
+- A signet node checks at startup that every block header it holds at a
+  retarget has the difficulty its current rule gives it. If one does not, it
+  refuses to start, names the lowest such header, and asks for the setting
+  that header was accepted under to be restored or for `-reindex`. That
+  catches a node given the option after it accepted a header at or above the
+  first retarget the option changes (when the two rules differ at that
+  retarget), and one whose option was removed or changed after it accepted
+  headers under it. A header is checked when it is first accepted, not when
+  the block index is loaded, and keeping such a header would let the node
+  follow a chain that a fresh node with the same rule rejects.
+- Removing or changing the option after the network has passed the first
+  retarget it changes takes the node off the network: it refuses to start
+  until the option is restored or the node is reindexed, and after `-reindex`
+  it rejects the network's blocks from the first retarget where the two rules
+  differ.
+
+The node logs `Signet difficulty retargets against N s per block from height H`
+at startup.
+
+The upper bound of 600 is where signet's `powLimit` stops leaving room for the
+retarget's arithmetic: it multiplies the old target by up to four times the
+expected period in 256 bits. At 2016 blocks of 600 s that still fits, and at
+601 s it would not.
diff --git a/src/chainparams.cpp b/src/chainparams.cpp
index 32c3bff..a9e2cea 100644
--- a/src/chainparams.cpp
+++ b/src/chainparams.cpp
@@ -18,6 +18,7 @@
 #include <cassert>
 #include <cstdint>
 #include <limits>
+#include <optional>
 #include <stdexcept>
 #include <vector>
 
@@ -39,6 +40,34 @@ void ReadSigNetArgs(const ArgsManager& args, CChainParams::SigNetOptions& option
         }
         options.challenge.emplace(*val);
     }
+    if (!args.GetArgs("-signetpowtargetspacing").empty()) {
+        const auto values = args.GetArgs("-signetpowtargetspacing");
+        if (values.size() != 1) {
+            throw std::runtime_error("-signetpowtargetspacing cannot be multiple values.");
+        }
+        if (!options.challenge) {
+            throw std::runtime_error("-signetpowtargetspacing requires -signetchallenge.");
+        }
+        const auto& value{values[0]};
+        const auto at{value.find('@')};
+        const auto spacing{ToIntegral<int64_t>(value.substr(0, at))};
+        const auto height{at == std::string::npos ? std::optional<int32_t>{0} : ToIntegral<int32_t>(value.substr(at + 1))};
+        if (!spacing || !height) {
+            throw std::runtime_error(strprintf("-signetpowtargetspacing must be <seconds>[@<height>], not '%s'.", value));
+        }
+        // Not longer than the signet default. The retarget multiplies the old
+        // target by up to four times the expected timespan in 256 bits, and
+        // signet's powLimit leaves room for exactly that at 2016 blocks of 600 s
+        // (sanity_check_chainparams in pow_tests.cpp); 601 s would overflow. The
+        // same bound keeps that factor inside the 32 bits arith_uint256 takes.
+        if (*spacing < 1 || *spacing > 10 * 60) {
+            throw std::runtime_error(strprintf("-signetpowtargetspacing must be between 1 and 600 seconds, not %d.", *spacing));
+        }
+        if (*height < 0) {
+            throw std::runtime_error(strprintf("-signetpowtargetspacing height must not be negative (%s).", value));
+        }
+        options.pow_target_spacing_change.emplace(Consensus::PowTargetSpacingChange{.height = *height, .spacing = *spacing});
+    }
 }
 
 void ReadRegTestArgs(const ArgsManager& args, CChainParams::RegTestOptions& options)
